WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.118
(rhythmic electric music)

00:00:02.118 --> 00:00:03.844
- [Voiceover] When you see
the players get the ball

00:00:03.844 --> 00:00:06.402
in their hand for the first
time it's a cross between

00:00:06.402 --> 00:00:08.402
intrigue and excitement.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.486
It's great to see 'em try and
bounce the ball and to see it

00:00:12.486 --> 00:00:14.592
actually bounce away.

00:00:14.592 --> 00:00:18.759
It can make the best of people
look really, really silly.

00:00:19.973 --> 00:00:21.588
(wild cheering)

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.892
- [Voiceover] The #1 sport in Australia

00:00:23.892 --> 00:00:26.135
is Australian Rules Football.

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:29.365
It's basically a cross
between rugby and soccer.

00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:31.782
And the fans go crazy for it.

00:00:32.853 --> 00:00:34.428
There's one problem.

00:00:34.428 --> 00:00:37.503
They don't have enough tall people.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:38.817
So what do they do?

00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:40.817
They come to the States.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:47.266
- This combines the US AFL
Combine and we started this

00:00:47.266 --> 00:00:48.671
four years ago.

00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:52.838
Basically in a search for
guys six-foot-seven and above.

00:00:54.051 --> 00:00:56.033
- [Voiceover] And these
tall American athletes,

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.097
they don't really need to
know a lot about Australia.

00:00:59.097 --> 00:01:01.184
- It's a home of the kangaroos, I think.

00:01:01.184 --> 00:01:03.177
- I know it's a lotta kangaroos.

00:01:03.177 --> 00:01:06.828
- I hear a lot about kangaroos
and spiders and snakes.

00:01:06.828 --> 00:01:09.375
- [Michael] In selecting these
athletes we predominantly

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:12.163
look for guys that are hungry.

00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:15.297
Most of the participants
predominantly come from basketball.

00:01:15.297 --> 00:01:18.346
The concept of basketball in
terms of the athlete being

00:01:18.346 --> 00:01:21.125
in traffic and having spatial
awareness and those sorts

00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:24.979
of things is really
transferable to our game.

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:27.156
- [Voiceover] Which is good
news because less than two percent

00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:30.924
of college basketball players
will make it to the pros.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.230
The Australian Football League
gives them another chance

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:37.053
to live out their dreams
of being a pro athlete.

00:01:37.053 --> 00:01:38.789
- [Michael] Most of the
participants are quite shocked

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:42.838
when they see the game for the first time.

00:01:42.838 --> 00:01:44.376
- [Voiceover] The question
is, what do the athletes

00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:45.876
think of all this?

00:01:47.753 --> 00:01:49.129
- When I got to come on invite I thought

00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:50.487
it was fake, actually.

00:01:50.487 --> 00:01:52.285
I thought it was a scam.

00:01:52.285 --> 00:01:54.264
- First thing I thought,
I thought it was a scam.

00:01:54.264 --> 00:01:57.027
- I thought they was contacting
the wrong person, actually.

00:01:57.027 --> 00:01:59.527
- What is Australian Football?

00:02:00.382 --> 00:02:02.234
- [Voiceover] Skepticism aside,
how do you teach these guys

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:05.295
a game they never even heard of before?

00:02:05.295 --> 00:02:07.378
- [Michael] So the Combine
kicks off in the early piece

00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:09.548
with a physical testing,
and then start to building

00:02:09.548 --> 00:02:13.563
to the skills, the basics
of hand-balling, the ability

00:02:13.563 --> 00:02:16.827
to see what they're like with their hands.

00:02:16.827 --> 00:02:19.030
Then we can start to get into
the more competitive stuff

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.603
where they might crash and
bash into each other which,

00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:23.482
they love that.

00:02:23.482 --> 00:02:26.149
(roaring crowd)

00:02:27.505 --> 00:02:29.723
- [Voiceover] This is Mason Cox.

00:02:29.723 --> 00:02:31.875
He played basketball at Oklahoma State.

00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:34.019
Two years ago, he was just
like one of these guys

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:35.382
on the Combine.

00:02:35.382 --> 00:02:38.643
Now, he's playing
professionally in Australia.

00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:41.420
- [Michael] They can be
one of the 22 superstars

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.670
out there on an AFL team.

00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:46.132
It's a fantastic opportunity
for these guys to continue

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.299
their professional career.

